A row flex item whose min-width is auto and whose overflow is visible has an automatic minimum width (CSS Flexbox
4.5): its min-content width, capped by a definite width (a replaced item's is its box width) and by its maximum.
Items shrank, and flex: 1 items grew from zero, below their content. An auto basis never falls below that
minimum, so it is measured only for a line that shrinks; another basis measures it for the hypothetical size.
A non-replaced item with a length width keeps no automatic minimum: its shrink-to-fit width is that length, so the
zero-width measure cannot see its content. Grid contributions, flex rows and the aspect-ratio automatic minimum
share that measure (LayoutDetails::GetMinContentWidth), taken once per layout pass for its element and inputs.

